{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39648984",
      "title": "It's All About Components! [Core Concept]",
      "sourceHash": "5d0f3e5aab34f0f4fabef3ee56f0fd2dd72f71dc60dac408120d8d71dea00c8f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 2.37,
          "en": "React and its ecosystem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 4.98,
          "en": "provide dozens of useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.98,
          "end": 7.89,
          "en": "and important features and concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "which, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "are all going to be covered in depth throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 19.49,
          "en": "But if you were forced to identify only one core concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "which you will need for all React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 28.05,
          "en": "it would be the concept of working with Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.05,
          "end": 33.05,
          "en": "Because Components are potentially reusable building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.72,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "which you, as a React developer, can create,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 38.55,
          "en": "and which you then combine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "to build the overall user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 47.63,
          "en": "So React apps are in the end built by combining Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 52.29,
          "en": "And whilst a couple of additional features and concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.29,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "would be required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 57.78,
          "en": "to create truly interactive user interfaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.78,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "Components are the one concept every React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 65.94,
          "en": "no matter its complexity, will use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.94,
          "end": 70.94,
          "en": "And indeed, the idea of thinking of user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "as combinations of Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "is not unique or exclusive to React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 80.16,
          "en": "If you visit any website of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.16,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "you'll quickly be able to identify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 84.72,
          "en": "a couple of key building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.72,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "that make up the overall site or app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 91.56,
          "en": "For example, in this demo website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.56,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "we're going to work on throughout this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 98.91,
          "en": "you could identify the header area, the key concept items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.91,
          "end": 103.62,
          "en": "and the interactive tabs section as Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 107.22,
          "en": "You could also identify more or less Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.22,
          "end": 110.31,
          "en": "because as you will also learn in this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.31,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "and this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "it will come down to the developers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 115.74000000000001,
          "en": "who are working on an app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 120.12,
          "en": "to define how big or small a component should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.12,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "But the idea behind those Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "really just is that they wrap HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 129.33,
          "en": "and possibly also CSS code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.33,
          "end": 132.6,
          "en": "as well as any related JavaScript logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.6,
          "end": 133.89,
          "en": "that might be needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.89,
          "end": 138.18,
          "en": "And together, those languages and code pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.18,
          "end": 141.543,
          "en": "then define and control a part of the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.5,
          "end": 145.44,
          "en": "This allows you, the developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.44,
          "end": 148.86,
          "en": "to split up complex user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.86,
          "end": 151.92000000000002,
          "en": "into smaller, more manageable parts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.92000000000002,
          "end": 153.93,
          "en": "which, at least potentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.93,
          "end": 158.04,
          "en": "may also be reused in different places of the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.04,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "For example, this core concept component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "is used four times, just configured with different data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 168.673,
          "en": "but using the same HTML markup and styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.673,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "and JavaScript logic under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 174.45,
          "en": "And that's one of the main reasons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.45,
          "end": 179.4,
          "en": "why this Components approach is so powerful and popular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.4,
          "end": 182.28,
          "en": "Without Components, you would quickly end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.28,
          "end": 186.66,
          "en": "with rather large and complex HTML files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.66,
          "end": 190.59,
          "en": "that may become difficult to navigate and work with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.59,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "In addition, change in your code might need to be applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "in different parts of your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 201.6,
          "en": "hence, increasing the likelihood of errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 201.6,
          "end": 203.82,
          "en": "When using this Components approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.82,
          "end": 205.77,
          "en": "you are instead reusing code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "and you only need to make such a change in one place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 212.76,
          "en": "Another big advantage of this Components idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.76,
          "end": 216.54,
          "en": "is that related code can be stored together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.54,
          "end": 218.49,
          "en": "Because without Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.49,
          "end": 223.17000000000002,
          "en": "you would typically have your markup in the HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.17000000000002,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "and your JavaScript code in one of your JavaScript files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 231.21,
          "en": "If you needed to make a change to the JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.21,
          "end": 233.91,
          "en": "you would therefore have to switch back and forth",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.91,
          "end": 236.25,
          "en": "between those files all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 239.31,
          "en": "And since you are likely working in different files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.31,
          "end": 241.59,
          "en": "and it's quite possible that you're not seeing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.59,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "all the related code together all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 245.91,
          "en": "it's also quite likely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.91,
          "end": 248.7,
          "en": "that you might accidentally break your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.7,
          "end": 252.03,
          "en": "because you may be changed something in your JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.03,
          "end": 254.64,
          "en": "that then would've also required a change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.64,
          "end": 256.5,
          "en": "in the HtML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.5,
          "end": 260.07,
          "en": "On the other hand, when working with Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.07,
          "end": 263.88,
          "en": "related code is typically kept closely together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.88,
          "end": 267.24,
          "en": "hence, simplifying the development process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 267.24,
          "end": 270.81,
          "en": "And the last major advantage of working with Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.81,
          "end": 274.38,
          "en": "is that you follow a design and development principle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.38,
          "end": 277.14,
          "en": "which is almost always a good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.14,
          "end": 279.93,
          "en": "You have a separation of concerns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.93,
          "end": 282.99,
          "en": "Different Components do different things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.99,
          "end": 285.003,
          "en": "and handle different parts of the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 286.11,
          "end": 289.26,
          "en": "For example, in the demo project of this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.26,
          "end": 291.6,
          "en": "we have Components that are responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.6,
          "end": 293.55,
          "en": "for outputting information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.55,
          "end": 295.74,
          "en": "and we have other Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.74,
          "end": 299.07,
          "en": "that are responsible for switching between tabs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.07,
          "end": 301.29,
          "en": "and handling user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.29,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "And that's, of course, just a basic app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 305.61,
          "en": "The more complex your projects become,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.61,
          "end": 307.8,
          "en": "the more useful this pattern becomes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.8,
          "end": 310.14,
          "en": "as it also simplifies the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.14,
          "end": 313.62,
          "en": "of working on the same project with multiple developers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.62,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "where every developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 318.57,
          "en": "works on their own feature area, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.57,
          "end": 322.62,
          "en": "And that's why this idea of working with Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 322.62,
          "end": 327.6,
          "en": "is embraced by React and why as a React developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.6,
          "end": 331.56,
          "en": "you will create and use hundreds and thousands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.56,
          "end": 334.83,
          "en": "of such Components, also in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 334.83,
          "end": 338.04,
          "en": "And just as a side note, it's not just React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 341.64,
          "en": "This concept is so popular and useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 341.64,
          "end": 343.35,
          "en": "that you'll also find it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 343.35,
          "end": 346.26,
          "en": "in other popular front-end frameworks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 346.26,
          "end": 349.17,
          "en": "like Angular, Vue, or Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 349.17,
          "end": 350.49,
          "en": "And you'll also find it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.49,
          "end": 353.34000000000003,
          "en": "outside the world of web development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.34000000000003,
          "end": 357.65999999999997,
          "en": "For example, in mobile development frameworks like Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 357.65999999999997,
          "end": 359.31,
          "en": "So let's therefore now take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 359.31,
          "end": 361.92,
          "en": "at our first React component in code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 361.92,
          "end": 365.493,
          "en": "and then, of course, also create our first component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}